hermes v0.22.5: the dashboard's self-hosted OIDC provider admits every
identity the issuer vouches for. Nothing in hermes checks group
membership (plugins/dashboard_auth/self_hosted: the `groups` claim only
becomes Session.org_id, a display string; still so in v0.22.5, no
allowed-groups option upstream, NousResearch/hermes-agent#55648), so the
issuer's own per-client restriction is the only authorization. An issuer
without one (dex) lets every account it knows into every agent's
dashboard.

Fix: `allowed_groups` (HERMES_DASHBOARD_OIDC_ALLOWED_GROUPS, or
dashboard.oauth.self_hosted.allowed_groups; comma list). When set, the
verified ID token's `groups` claim must name one of them. The check sits
in _verify_id_token (= _claims_for), which every path that makes a
Session goes through: the login callback (JwtOAuthProvider.complete_login
-> _grant: 400, no session cookie), each refresh (refresh_session ->
_grant: RefreshExpiredError, the session ends) and the per-request
re-verification of the stored ID token (verify_session -> _claims_for:
None, refresh, then re-login). The issuer emits `groups` only for the
`groups` scope, so the deployment asks for it. Unset, nothing changes.

